  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Hamilcone and HEp-2 through a series of target interactions. Hamilcone is implicated as a target of three different compounds—Desacetylbufotalin-3-O-Sulfite, Kanzonol H, and Cornusalterin F—all of which are predicted to interact with HEp-2. These compounds are likely acting as modulators or inhibitors of the Macrophage-expressed gene 1 protein, which is the common target across all three pathways. The scores from the predictions indicate a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, with the highest score (0.5529) for Desacetylbufotalin-3-O-Sulfite and the next highest for Kanzonol H and Cornusalterin F. The shared target of these compounds at the Macrophage-expressed gene 1 protein suggests a possible mechanism by which Hamilcone may influence HEp-2, potentially through the regulation of this gene. However, the evidence is not definitive, and further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the biological relevance of these interactions.",
